  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-24T00:55:53.957Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "Rzi+rdXkQj3MMSPHNmnXMN4UwgLQqp0xGZL8oN3XbK1DQPdVa5ohXeneDw0anXmPriRnqQ02o4M2ScarPntoHQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 206318,
  "published": "2026-07-24T00:53:47.603Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.7: consumer-driven upgrade cycle closing 26 divergence gaps (G1–G26) from a live multi-tenant integration — multi-tenant/background execution, schema/DbContext ownership, identity/personas, the permission decision point, wiring/hosting, first-class impersonation, and localization of MyIdentity's own messages. Contains breaking changes: service DI signatures (MyIdentityMessageDescriber, IMyIdentityContextProvider), the HasAnyPermissionInScopeAsync→HasAnyAssignmentInScopeAsync rename (old name changed meaning), EnableDataProtection now defaults true, config validation moved to start-time, GetAllAsync excludes Deleted by default, noLockout bool→bool?, CreateAsync→Task<TTenant>, MyIdentitySeedDataAsync stops migrating (add MyIdentityMigrateAsync), and ~15 input-guard sites now throw MyIdentityCustomException instead of ArgumentException. See UPGRADE.md §12–§18 for the full changelog and migration steps. API may still change before stable.",
